    "created_at": "2023-04-21T06:12:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T06:19:08Z",
    "body": "@annevk \r\n1- Don't you think we should be more accurate here and say “document tree”? After all this the type of node tree you get from parsing HTML, if my understanding is correct.\r\n\r\n2- I think Bathos made a very good point when he said the term “DOM tree” is popular among devs. I think we should still define this term somewhere (maybe in the DOM spec?)",
