    "created_at": "2023-04-21T06:29:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T06:29:25Z",
    "body": "Some instances could maybe use document tree. It's not more accurate per se, it just asserts that the root is a document, which isn't the case for everything HTML does.\r\n\r\nThere are a lot of things that are popular that are not necessarily correct. Some we say something about, e.g., \"HTML5\", but I'm not convinced DOM tree is up there. DOM as a term is used for a lot of things, so avoiding it and using more precise terms seems better.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
